                                                                        ] ;
                                                        rdfs:comment "Soil depth rootable refers to the depth of soil that is capable of supporting plant roots, excluding impenetrable layers such as bedrock or compacted zones. This is an important factor for determining agricultural suitability. Source: Soil Science Society of America. (2008). Soil Science Glossary. Soil Science Society of America." ;
                                                        rdfs:label "SoilDepthRootable"@en ;
                                                        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "ISRIC Report 2019/01: Tier 1 and Tier 2 data in the context of the federated Global Soil Information System. Appendix 1"@en .


